From fcb8e7a3ceacfc9079a7b62313653bfb1ae06bf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:34:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 51/53] moe cache: batched decode admissions, one layer step =
 two kernels (GGML_MOE_FILL_BATCH)

Inside one moe_cache_remap_dev call the victim saves, fills, cold pointer writes and map uploads of a layer are queued and
launched just before the remap: phase 1 the saves, phase 2 the fills.  Same bytes and pointers, fewer dispatches.
GGML_MOE_FILL_BATCH=0: one launch per copy and pointer as before.  GGML_MOE_FILL_BATCH_FAULT=n: the n-th flush fails.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu | 295 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 273 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

